d any damage. Instead of sharing these videos here, please forward them directly to the Police.\nThank you.\n3\nRespect everyone's privacy\n\ud83d\udea8 Group Reminder: Respect Privacy & GDPR Compliance \ud83d\udea8\nPlease do not share residents' addresses, personal details, or any safeguarding concerns in this group. Doing so may breach GDPR regulations and compromise individuals' privacy.\nThis group thrives on mutual trust. While authentic and expressive discussions are encouraged, they may involve sensitive or private matters. Let's all commit to keeping what's shared here confidential and within the group.\nThank you.\n4\nBe kind and courteous towards all members\n\ud83d\udeab Group Conduct Policy \ud83d\udeab\nTo maintain a respectful and inclusive environment, the following behaviours are strictly prohibited:\n- Swearing or use of offensive language\n- Degrading or belittling others\n- Sarcastic or inflammatory comments\n- Bullying, harassment, or racism\nAny member found engaging in these behaviours will receive a warning. Continued violations will result in an immediate ban from the group.\nLet\u2019s keep this space safe, supportive, and welcoming for everyone\n5\nNo Businesses, Lost Pets Or Deliveries\nSelf-promotion, spam and irrelevant links aren't allowed.\nThis group is for neighbourhood safety and residents information, not lost Pets or Parcels nor business advertising.\nPlease do post on your own Facebook page, as this will reach the public, this group is closed and private, so, non members will not see anything if you tag them in posts.\nThank you.\n6\nPlease do not private message other members\n\ud83d\udeab No Unsolicited Private Messages\nTo maintain a respectful and safe environment, do not send private messages to other members without their prior consent. This helps prevent spam, unwanted contact, and potential harassment.\n\ud83d\udd12 Zero Tolerance Policy\nAny member found violating this rule and reported will receive an instant ban\u2014